Troubleshooting Narrative:

What went wrong across the queue, or what was the most significant issue you encountered?
The most significant issue across the queue was the differnece between the user symptoms and the actual state of the local machine. Rather than dealing with a broken system, the primary challenge was investigating and proving a that the workstation was actually healthy without dismissing the users reports.

What evidence did you check first, and why?
For each ticket, I immediately checked the objective, built in Windows diagnostic tools.

What did you try on each ticket?
On Ticket A, I searched the Local Users and Groups console to locate the locked account. On Ticket B, I sorted Task Manager by CPU and Memory to locate any resource-heavy processes. On Ticket C, I expanded the audio controllers in Device Manager to look for warning icons or missing drivers. On Ticket D, I ran ipconfig /all and a ping to test the network stack from the loopback address out to the external internet.

What resolved each issue, or what would you try next if you could not resolve it?
Because no faults were present on the machine, no system changes were applied to resolve the tickets.
